WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:09.600
Welcome to “Introduction to Project Management.”

2
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.660
Are you interested in learning about project
management?

3
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.040
Do you want to learn more about what project
managers do and how to become one?

4
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.840
Maybe you’re just starting and not sure
what project management is or even what counts

5
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.260
as a project.

6
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:27.240
If you’re curious about project management,
the responsibilities of a project manager,

7
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.460
the skills required to become one, and careers
in project management, then this course is

8
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:32.880
for you.

9
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.160
Project management refers to the tools and
methodologies used to plan and execute projects.

10
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.540
Projects can be anything from the development
of an app to the construction of a bridge.

11
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.880
The important thing is that projects involve
tasks that must be accomplished to achieve

12
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.440
a goal and produce some value.

13
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.940
Nowadays, project management is a more valuable
skill than ever.

14
00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:59.220
We live in a project-based economy, in which
projects are the most common method of dividing

15
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.660
work and producing value.

16
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.100
Having project management skills makes you
an attractive candidate for many jobs.

17
00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.600
Project manager roles are expected to only
grow over the next ten years.

18
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.900
This course is divided into four modules.

19
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:18.120
First, you’ll learn the very basics of project
management, like what project management is.

20
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.860
In the second, you’ll learn about the role
played by project managers in the workplace,

21
00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.060
different project management methodologies,
and current trends in project management.

22
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:33.180
Next, the course will cover the skills and
responsibilities expected of a project manager.

23
00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.580
The final module will describe different career
opportunities in project management, so you

24
00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.600
will be prepared to progress in your project
management career after finishing this course.

25
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.540
This course uses various teaching methods,
including videos, readings, activities, quizzes,

26
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.020
a final project, and interviews with project
management experts.

27
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.780
Let’s briefly hear these experts introduce
themselves.

28
00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.780
You will hear more from them as the course
progresses.

29
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.240
Hi, I'm Greg Kuya.

30
00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.560
I'm a project manager with over 20 years of
experience and I'm currently working on my

31
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.060
own project called Planet Earth Things.

32
00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.440
We make Social Impact games.

33
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.380
Hello, my name is Kathern Brooks.

34
00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.960
I'm a senior project manager at Zscaler.

35
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:19.020
Hi, my name is Erica Maldonado, and I'm a
program manager at Coursera.

36
00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:26.940
Hi, I'm Kasie and I currently work as a business
consultant as well as a subject matter expert

37
00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.200
doing course development.

38
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:34.200
In the past, I've worked as a business consultant
doing project management and program management

39
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.580
for large companies

40
00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.900
as well as helping companies
do agile transformations

41
00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.260
where they move from a
waterfall project management

42
00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.380
methodology to an agile methodology.

43
00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.860
Hello everyone!
My name is Daniel Yeomans.

44
00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:54.360
I'm currently a subject matter expert working
with Skill Up Technologies.

45
00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.240
However, I'm also a professor.

46
00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:02.280
I work for about four different universities
in the greater Seattle area.

47
00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:08.640
I do continuing education, I do corporate
training, and in addition, I also perform

48
00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.260
course development.

49
00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.880
Once you have completed this course, you will
receive a badge and certificate that can be

50
00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.300
shared with prospective employers to demonstrate
your knowledge of project management.

51
00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:22.740
Get ready for the next step in your project
management journey, and good luck!